{{UPGRADE_NOTES}}

Workbench icons in this archive:

All four program icons (raptor.info, raptor_nofpu.info, raptor_030.info
and raptor_030_fpu.info) contain two further inactive ToolTypes next to
the existing launch options:

    (CD32 options: ON | OFF)
    (CD32=OFF)

Both are enclosed in parentheses, so the game ignores them and the cd32
value from amiga.cfg is used (OFF by default). They document the option
and do not change saved settings.

To enable a CD32 pad from an icon:

1. Open the icon information window (Icons / Information...).
2. Replace "(CD32=OFF)" with the active line CD32=ON, without
   parentheses. Keep exactly one CD32 entry - do not add a second one.
3. Joystick input must be enabled. The shipped icons already contain
   JOYSTICK=ON. If an icon contains JOYSTICK=OFF, replace it with
   JOYSTICK=ON, and remove an active NOJOY entry or put it in
   parentheses: (NOJOY).
4. Save the icon and start the game again.

The CD32 ToolType overrides amiga.cfg for that launch only and is never
written back. CD32=OFF selects the ordinary 1/2/3-button joystick path
and does not disable controller input.

The game renders in a fixed 320x200, 8-bit paletted mode on a dedicated
screen. Four native m68k binaries are provided:

- raptor         : 68060 with FPU (recommended)
- raptor_nofpu   : 68060/68EC060/68LC060 soft-float
- raptor_030_fpu : 68030 with external 68881/68882 FPU
- raptor_030     : 68030 soft-float

Sound effects are played through AHI (ahi.device) at the native 11025 Hz
16-bit stereo rate. Music can be played via several backends:

- ADLIB  : lightweight OPL3 emulation (mixed into the AHI stream)
- CAMD   : General MIDI via camd.library (external synth / software synth)
- MHI    : MP3 music via hardware decoder
- WAVE   : pre-decoded WAV files mixed into the AHI stream
- OFF    : no music (the default)

Select from CLI with -music=mhi or from a Workbench icon with the MUSIC=MHI
ToolType. For MHI, MP3 files are read from MP3/. Raptor first tries its
explicit driver candidates while preserving the optional MHIDRIVER=<driver>
override and fallback scan of LIBS:MHI/#?.library.

MP3PRELOAD=OFF is the default and keeps the original MHI path, streaming
the MP3 during playback. MP3PRELOAD=ON loads the complete MP3 into memory
before playback; playback then uses resident MP3 data with no MP3 disk
I/O. This option only affects MHI.

Joystick input is enabled by default on port 1 (DB9, the second physical
Amiga port) and requires lowlevel.library v40+. The optional CD32 gamepad
can be enabled with "cd32 = ON" in amiga.cfg or with the CD32=ON startup
parameter (CLI -cd32=on or icon ToolType CD32=ON), which overrides the
file for that launch only and is never written back (disabled by default).
Each of the seven pad buttons has its own assignment (FIRE,
SPECIAL_SELECT, MEGA_BOMB, PAUSE, CANCEL or NONE); the yellow button
defaults to CANCEL and the play button is PAUSE. In the shop
SPECIAL_SELECT toggles BUY/SELL, FIRE confirms and CANCEL backs out.
Workbench icon ToolTypes are supported (GFX, VIDEO, MUSIC, MOUSE, JOYSTICK,
CD32, etc.). Persistent audio volumes are stored in amiga.cfg in the game
directory; saving updates the file in place and preserves manual edits,
comments and CD32 / joystick button assignments.

